# Project Rules — Photography Platform

## Stack & Architecture
- **Frontend & API:** Next.js (App Router, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS) in `src/`, deployed on Vercel.
- **Database & Auth:** Supabase (PostgreSQL + Supabase Auth via `@supabase/ssr`).
- **Storage & CDN:** Private AWS S3 bucket (`/masters/` for raw high-res files, `/proofs/` for watermarked display assets) + AWS CloudFront pointing **only** to `/proofs/*`.
- **Image Processing:** Isolated AWS Lambda in `aws/lambda/watermark/` using `sharp` and `@aws-sdk/client-s3`. Keep completely decoupled from the root Next.js build.
- **Payments:** Stripe Checkout + verified Stripe Webhooks.

## Non-Negotiable Security & Data Rules
1. **Never proxy photo uploads or downloads through Next.js API routes.** Always issue short-lived S3 pre-signed PUT/GET URLs so browsers transfer files directly to/from S3.
2. **Never expose `/masters/*` via CloudFront or public URLs.** Clean high-res masters are served strictly via time-limited S3 pre-signed GET URLs after server-side entitlement verification.
3. **Never trust client redirects for payment confirmation.** Order status and download quotas may ONLY be updated inside `/api/stripe/webhook` after verifying `Stripe-Signature`.
4. **Enforce RBAC in both code and database.** Use Supabase Row-Level Security (RLS) on every table AND verify `profiles.role === 'admin'` server-side on all admin API routes and actions.
5. **Keep `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY`, `AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY`, and `STRIPE_SECRET_KEY` strictly server-side.** Never import `src/lib/supabase/admin.ts` into Client Components (`'use client'`).
6. **Watermarking happens in Lambda, never via CSS alone.** Client-side protections (`contextmenu`, `user-select: none`) are secondary speed bumps only.

## Workflow & Code Hygiene (16 GB RAM Friendly)
- Stay strictly within the scope of the current phase prompt. Do not scaffold or implement future phases prematurely.
- Prefer Server Components by default; add `'use client'` only for interactive components (uploaders, proofing selectors, forms).
- Use strict TypeScript with generated Supabase types (`src/types/database.ts`). Avoid `any`.
- After every task, run `npx tsc --noEmit` and `npm run lint` to verify zero errors before finishing.